From: Guangshuo Li <lgs201920130244@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:20:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iio: accel: kxcjk-1013: Disable autosuspend on remove
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.63
Git-commit: 1de1206a42741adfb72ca8b37dc71a6bc80cb074

[ Upstream commit 1de1206a42741adfb72ca8b37dc71a6bc80cb074 ]

kxcjk1013_probe() enables runtime PM autosuspend with
pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(). The probe error path correctly undoes
this setting with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(), but the normal
remove path only disables runtime PM.

The runtime PM API requires pm_runtime_use_autosuspend() to be undone
with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() at driver exit unless runtime PM
was enabled with devm_pm_runtime_enable(). Leaving the autosuspend flag
set therefore leaves the runtime PM state incompletely cleaned up after
the driver is unbound.

Add the missing pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() call to the remove
path.

This issue was found by manual code inspection.

Fixes: 124e1b1d0924 ("iio: accel: kxcjk-1013: support runtime pm")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Guangshuo Li <lgs201920130244@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Joshua Crofts <joshua.crofts1@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Srinivas Pandruvada <srinivas.pandruvada@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Cameron <jonathan.cameron@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 drivers/iio/accel/kxcjk-1013.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/accel/kxcjk-1013.c b/drivers/iio/accel/kxcjk-1013.c
index 297853cd39e5..a8652bdd011a 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/accel/kxcjk-1013.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/accel/kxcjk-1013.c
@@ -1548,6 +1548,7 @@ static void kxcjk1013_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 
 	iio_device_unregister(indio_dev);
 
+	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&client->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&client->dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&client->dev);
 
